## Common thread-pool diagnostics

- Pinned common Java source declares `ThreadPoolMonitor`,
  `ThreadPoolWrapper`, and `ThreadPoolStatusMonitor`. Rust has no matching
  utility types.
- A production source search across pinned client, remoting, and common Java
  sources found no client/remoting use of the monitor; references are confined
  to its common-package implementation.
- Source SHA-256 values: `91a953b534d3a753d2b1085cb08705cfd212ebd5e5fd7a7c5a254608fd155df9`
  (`ThreadPoolMonitor.java`),
  `244773886ec16a908ab031b447951070d74a2cae9abe20e49b982f9741ec4f76`
  (`ThreadPoolWrapper.java`), and
  `d8d9983890425406e26665e357a45186b7ec8ca9cb194135dfb6a7c7b0e86c2a`
  (`ThreadPoolStatusMonitor.java`).
- The diagnostic utility remains an unimplemented public common API; this
  disposition only establishes the lack of client/remoting execution call
  sites.

